/-!
# Structurality from `Equation4434` through a two-guard companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell2.py`.  `Equation4434` is `x ◇ (y ◇ x) = (x ◇ x) ◇ z`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with `x □ y = if a = b then (M.op a b) else if (M.op b a) = b then (M.op a a) else (M.op a b)` is an automorphism of `◇` --
is `GuardAut2_x_y_pyx_y_pxy_pxx_pxy_Equation4434`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation names no target, so every
law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
are 2 of them below.
-/

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language Law Law.MagmaLaw FreeMagma

set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
